I think bu'a/bu'e/bu'i would be much much much more useful if Lojban were a
second order language, because then we could talk about the existence of
predicates with desired properties in a non-stilted fashion. As a first
order language, though, with second order mechanisms requiring stilted
language, I don't think bu'a/bu'e/bu'i are especially useful.

mu'o mi'e latros

